# Build Verification

After making substantive code changes (new files, renamed exports, changed types, modified imports, updated configs), run the build to catch errors early:

```bash
npm run build
```

If the build fails, fix all errors before considering the task complete. Common issues:
- Missing or incorrect imports
- TypeScript type errors
- Invalid Next.js route exports
- Unused variables in strict mode

Also run the linter after changes:

```bash
npm run lint
```

When fixing build or lint errors, do NOT weaken TypeScript strictness or add `@ts-ignore` / `eslint-disable` unless there is a genuine reason. Fix the root cause instead.
